Hopefully this isn't a distraction, but if sigma is large enough relative to the width of the peninsula, you can't observe captures across the full range of the detection function along the minor axis of the peninsula, but you can along the major axis, leading sigma to be underestimated and density to be overestimated.  If the width of the peninsula is say, 6sigma or less (not sure exactly when you'll start seeing bias), you may start to run into problems.  Maybe this is consistent with your simulation results.

